 <section aria-labelledby="limits-title">
  <h2 id="limits-title">What this does not show</h2>
  <ul>
   <li><strong>Two models, one effort setting, through CLIs:</strong> these are not raw API tests or a compute-matched family comparison. A different wrapper, output allowance or model version could change coverage and cost.</li>
   <li><strong>A finite, exposed benchmark:</strong> the original tasks are public, so contamination is possible. Local actors and screens are fixed, tasks repeat, and Work or Proof and Signal share trajectories. This is not broad evidence about all agent work.</li>
   <li><strong>Ceilings are not equivalence:</strong> GPT’s perfect fleet choices leave no observed room for examples to help. Zero differences do not establish equal capabilities or effects on harder tasks.</li>
   <li><strong>GPT usage is “as reported by the CLI”:</strong> hidden computation was not independently enumerated, and there is no GPT USD figure. Subscription, hardware, energy and opportunity costs are not zero merely because cash allocation is unavailable.</li>
   <li><strong>Transport overhead can decide a budgeted result:</strong> GPT’s Work or Proof failure concerns this fixed allowance and wrapper. It does not show that its unconstrained judgments cannot identify breaches. A new budget or adapter needs a new registered comparison.</li>
   <li><strong>The correction is not blind:</strong> A9 follows inspection of A8. It restores registered failure scoring while leaving A8 visible; Claude’s door coverage still prevents a scientific verdict. A new, prospectively registered test with adequate output room could resolve that gap.</li>
  </ul>
 </section>
